=== Generated Answer (model draft; check against evidence) ===
Labels for trolls are obtained either by manual labeling (supervised scenario) or, when such labels are unavailable, by propagating labels of news media outlets they mention (distant supervision scenario).

In the fully supervised task T1, the label for each troll user is available for training thanks to manual labeling [4]. In the more realistic distant supervision scenario, labels for troll accounts are assumed unavailable, so the paper leverages labels of more persistent entities, news media, and propagates them to trolls through the citation/mention graph: LEFT→left, RIGHT→right, CENTER→news feed, e.g., via a proxy model for media or label propagation [3][6][7][8]. This propagation allows inferring the final labeling on the accounts without any manual labeling [8].
